{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1153869-eternus-a-discipline-based-on-immortality-homebrew","id":1153869,"title":"Eternus: A discipline based on immortality (homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-28T21:17:14-07:00","id":1153869,"title":"Eternus: A discipline based on immortality (homebrew)","content":"So, I've been thinking lately about Vampires and time-related effects. For those like me that do a lot of crossover, it's definitely a blind spot in the Vampiric repetoire; when Changelings, Mages, and Demons mess with Time, Vampires tend to be pretty screwed, beyond the occasional ability to do something like using Celerity to counteract being slowed down temporarily.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, most relegate such things to odd Bloodlines or very rarely to something like an elder devotion that kinda-sorta does something semi-similar, and it means that it's still something most Vampires will never see.<br /> <br /> Why? The most common answer is that most universally accessible Disciplines are an extension of natural Vampiric abilities; their physical intensity evolves into physical disciplines, their aura into mental disciplines, etcetera. And, well, it IS a good point. Most don't think of Vampiric abilities as giving any real grasp of the timeline or the flow of time, after all.<br /> <br /> So, then I thought: But, they DO have a natural vampiric ability that has to deal with Time. Immortality. They naturally don't age, their bodies aren't subject to decay, and their memories often can grow immeasurably to allow them to recall long stretches of existence.<br /> <br /> So thus, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f_HQuF-OeaH4iGxcf2jcZnXikjThCyLQaL2xOYOzWCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Eternus</a> was born. Eternus is a Discipline involving taking Kindred Immortality and wielding it. It's not time magic, allowing time to be sped up or slowed down, it's not fae trickery allowing you to age someone or keep them forever young. It's taking a Kindred's immortal, unyielding imprint on the timeline and making it even <i>stronger</i>. Their sense of their existence perfects, their place within the timeline doesn't budge, and yes, at the upper levels they even learn to decide that small fragments of their timeline need to be revisited and readjusted.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll give the disclaimer ahead of time: I'm well aware that the lower levels especially are very crossover focused and won't do much except against the aforementioned splats and other Kindred with the same Discipline, although I tried to be sure every level has at least SOME use in a Kindred's nightly Requiem, however minor.<br /> I'm also aware that a lot of these levels do take some heavy inspiration from certain other splats' powers, but I did try to vamp them up a bit (open to suggestions to further tweak that, though).<br /> <br /> So, lemme know what you all think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>(By the way, I fully admit that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> 's new bloodline and take on Temporis <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1149105-bloodline-conversion-homebrew-the-elois-and-temporis\">here</a> is what got me thinking down the line of actually creating something, but this is meant to fill a slightly different niche)</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T23:31:30-07:00","id":1153881,"title":"","content":"I feel as though the esoteric nature of this powerset and its basis in extending the implications of a specific vampiric quality for power makes it better-suited as a Coil; failing that, the design principle behind Disciplines in 2e is such that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121408#post1121408\">the first dot in the Discipline should let you do the thing the Discipline's known for</a>. What is Eternus known for doing, and what makes it horrifying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T09:43:55-07:00","id":1153935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1153869-eternus-a-discipline-based-on-immortality-homebrew?p=1153881#post1153881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the esoteric nature of this powerset and its basis in extending the implications of a specific vampiric quality for power makes it better-suited as a Coil; failing that, the design principle behind Disciplines in 2e is such that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121408#post1121408\">the first dot in the Discipline should let you do the thing the Discipline's known for</a>. What is Eternus known for doing, and what makes it horrifying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I didn't want to go the Coil route because 1) It's covenant-dependent and 2) Coils tend to be entirely internal, and this does eventually allow for a bit of an 'external' influence beyond what makes sense, to me, for a Coil to do.<br /> <br /> As for the guiding principle, I did have that kept in mind. The idea behind Eternus is it's what gives you control over your immortal thread. And at dot one, you're inherently able to sweep away changes to your perfected memory and retain a full knowledge of what has happened and what SHOULD have happened to you, even if it's been tampered with. As for being horrifying, it takes on the concept of their immortality and permanence and not only makes it more reliable, but makes it unyielding. I do recognize that from a mortal perspective, that isn't really recognizable until level 3+, when they're attempting to disable the vampire only to have their immortal nature remain unyielding to all attempts, but it's there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T12:29:52-07:00","id":1153956,"title":"","content":"Is there a particular reason why the first dot has no cost, is instant, and lasts all night (does it not work during the day?) with no dice roll?<br /> <br /> Is there any reason you wouldn't just have it on always?<br /> <br /> If it's effectively passive, why not just make it passive?<br /> <br /> And if it's passive, it's probably better as a merit with Eternus as a prerequisite, if you don't want a Coil. Disciplines are active, as far as I know. Some way for the Beast to enforce its will on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":". 10-29-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T12:49:38-07:00","id":1153961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1153869-eternus-a-discipline-based-on-immortality-homebrew?p=1153956#post1153956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a particular reason why the first dot has no cost, is instant, and lasts all night (does it not work during the day?) with no dice roll?<br /> <br /> Is there any reason you wouldn't just have it on always?<br /> <br /> If it's effectively passive, why not just make it passive?<br /> <br /> And if it's passive, it's probably better as a merit with Eternus as a prerequisite, if you don't want a Coil. Disciplines are active, as far as I know. Some way for the Beast to enforce its will on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Night&quot; is used by i'm pretty sure every single vampiric power that lasts a 'day', as a vampire thing. I always figured that meant it'd be active during the following day if they stayed awake, but I don't think that's ever been clarified.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the duration is for balance purposes; being heavily dependent on a Clash of Wills, I didn't want the level 1 power always getting the +4 benefit of a permanent power. +1 seemed more reasonable.<br /> <br /> I also was considering a slight drawback for having it active at the time, but couldn't think of something that fit what i was looking for (basically something that's not just a silly dice penalty, and that a Vampire would <b>feel</b> but yet would inure themselves to after a while as they progressed in the discipline and wanted the benefits more &quot;permanently&quot;). Open to suggestions there, though.<br /> <br /> And since it, like most level 1 powers, is built on and utilized by the further levels, it definitely can't be turned into a merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T21:13:42-07:00","id":1154055,"title":"","content":"This is almost exactly Temporis from the classic world of darkness, it's a nice idea but it could be messy...<br /> <br /> My take on it is that you make a bloodline centered around time control and give them Celerity + Dominate devotions, their trick is that they can go forward or back in time for only minutes or seconds before, along with temporarily stopping or slowing time in which they move unhindered. If we go as far as giving them history rewriting powers it would break the game.<br /> <br /> Also since Vampire is mostly a social/political game the ability to go back in time and think before you open your mouth is so devastatingly overpowered all by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T14:26:43-07:00","id":1154224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1153869-eternus-a-discipline-based-on-immortality-homebrew?p=1154055#post1154055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is almost exactly Temporis from the classic world of darkness, it's a nice idea but it could be messy...<br /> <br /> My take on it is that you make a bloodline centered around time control and give them Celerity + Dominate devotions, their trick is that they can go forward or back in time for only minutes or seconds before, along with temporarily stopping or slowing time in which they move unhindered. If we go as far as giving them history rewriting powers it would break the game.<br /> <br /> Also since Vampire is mostly a social/political game the ability to go back in time and think before you open your mouth is so devastatingly overpowered all by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could potentially see replacing the 4th dot entirely with something more immediate and making time travel at all an elder devotion. Would have to think on it. I do know time travel is a can of worms in ANY gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T00:00:35-07:00","id":1154304,"title":"","content":"I'm not a good judge of ST system mechanics, but from a first principles perspective - and going from an interpretation of the Discipline as projecting the immortality of the vampire into the world as an unchanging constant pillar of the world - the things it seems appropriate for it to be able to do are:<ul><li>Perfect memory of the vampire's past, and resistance to having it tampered with (including by environmental means, so the vampire will never be one of those who has their memories scrambled by torpor).. Ie your dot 1 power, whether you make it that, a 1 dot Devotion, or a Merit as Maina suggests.<br /> A possible drawback for this might be that the fleeting, growing life of the human who came before is an affront to the eternal vampire nature, and while the vampire can remember their unlife perfectly, they can barely remember their human life at all (I'll revisiit this later).</li> <li>The ability to recall and reproduce an action from their past. Something like your Eternal Perfection power - but on atmosphere, I'd say put it in the core Discipline rather than making it a Devotion. Also, have you considered turning the process round: after the original action, the vampire has to pay a vitae and make a roll (instant action) to fix it into themselves, making it a true part of their immortality?<br /> (While it would be tempting to do this with combat rolls, as an instant action, it could be dangerous to try, unless the action being fixed ended the combat).<br /> Later, the action can be recalled for another vitae as a reflexive action.<br /> Possible limitations might be that that you can only fix one or two actions per level of Blood Potency, and/or that you can't get beats from a repeated action.<br /> (With both limits, this power could be appropriate at a much lower level).</li> <li>The vampire's environment becoming unchanging. On an active level, that could include the Escape the Inevitable power. On a passive level, I'd also credit it with being able to maintain the vampire's Haven in an undecaying state, and all dots spent on Haven can act in some way (&quot;in some way&quot; meaning I'm not sure how to represent it) to resist damage to it. Also on a passive level, this could protect a torpored vampire's surroundings.</li> <li>The ability to inflict a crushing despair on any mortal who tries to harm the vampire - &quot;this is an immortal thing, bigger than you, older than you, and will be here long after you're gone, how can you hope to stand against it?&quot; - not fear, exactly, that's for Nightmare - but making it existentially hard to try. It could affect mortal supernaturals, but immortal beings should be immune.</li> <li>Precognitive glimpses of the vampire's future - as an unchanging pillar of immortality, all moments of the vampire's existence are one, so the senses that remember their past can be extended to the future as well.</li> <li>The Destined Future Power - as an unchanging pillar of immortality, the vampire bends the fleeting world around itself, drawing events into a pattern according to its will - this means that the future the vampire causes will tend to manifest as circumstances and coincidences more than the vampire's efforts being successful (the world is changing, not the vampire).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Things that make more sense to me as Devotions:<ul><li>Affecting the past. I don't think Chosen Past is the right way to do it exactly, though - if the Discipline draws on the immortality of the vampire, changing the course of their own history seems to weaken the source. Instead, what if they can go back, and &quot;step out&quot; of their timeline, interacting with the world beyond their own actions? As far as that period is concerned, the vampire would be in two places at once - the future self can't affect (or would suffer consequences for affecting) events for their past self, but can interact with the past in other ways, including discovering information and changing the fleeting history of the mortal world. Elders only.</li> <li>Permanence. An always on protection from someone doing the preceding to them. (Which would also act against mages, changelings, or the like doing it to them).</li> <li>Temporal Stasis. Which could in theory act as torpor as well, but with vastly more protection.</li> <li>And of course whatever of the preceding list doesn't make it into the main five.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>And Lastly:</b><br /> <br /> Baldaam once said that when you have a Discipline that any vampire can do, but which is signature for no clan, that suggests an unknown clan. So long as, I suppose, that you can posit a suitable &quot;vampire as...&quot; for it. Which in this case you can. Daevas are vampires as magents of seduction, Gangrel are vampires as savage predators, Mekhet are vampires as occult menace, Nosferatu are vampires as terrors in the shadows, and Venture are vampires as dread lords - but a clan with Eternus can be vampires as the weight of history, which seems both distinct and fitting to the concept of vampires.<br /> <br /> You want to be them because the're eternal - immutable - part of the fabric of the world itself. That's of course also why you should fear them. They should fear themselves because they forget to live - forget what life <i>is</i>.<br /> Losing memories of their mortal life would make sense as the weakness for this clan, making Humanity harder to hold on to.<br /> <br /> Legendary origins might include something to do with the Greek Titans - thrown down by the gods, but too much part of the world to be destroyed, so they endure. Or for the Once Upon a Midnight Darkly collection, well, who do you think first told that story - who was <i>there</i> for ever part of it?<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, Resilience and Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edited to Add:</b><br /> <br /> Whatever else can be said, I find this Discipline very evocative on a conceptual level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 10-31-2017, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T14:59:17-07:00","id":1154522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1153869-eternus-a-discipline-based-on-immortality-homebrew?p=1154304#post1154304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a good judge of ST system mechanics, but from a first principles perspective - and going from an interpretation of the Discipline as projecting the immortality of the vampire into the world as an unchanging constant pillar of the world - the things it seems appropriate for it to be able to do are:<ul><li>Perfect memory of the vampire's past, and resistance to having it tampered with (including by environmental means, so the vampire will never be one of those who has their memories scrambled by torpor).. Ie your dot 1 power, whether you make it that, a 1 dot Devotion, or a Merit as Maina suggests.<br /> A possible drawback for this might be that the fleeting, growing life of the human who came before is an affront to the eternal vampire nature, and while the vampire can remember their unlife perfectly, they can barely remember their human life at all (I'll revisiit this later).</li> <li>The ability to recall and reproduce an action from their past. Something like your Eternal Perfection power - but on atmosphere, I'd say put it in the core Discipline rather than making it a Devotion. Also, have you considered turning the process round: after the original action, the vampire has to pay a vitae and make a roll (instant action) to fix it into themselves, making it a true part of their immortality?<br /> (While it would be tempting to do this with combat rolls, as an instant action, it could be dangerous to try, unless the action being fixed ended the combat).<br /> Later, the action can be recalled for another vitae as a reflexive action.<br /> Possible limitations might be that that you can only fix one or two actions per level of Blood Potency, and/or that you can't get beats from a repeated action.<br /> (With both limits, this power could be appropriate at a much lower level).</li> <li>The vampire's environment becoming unchanging. On an active level, that could include the Escape the Inevitable power. On a passive level, I'd also credit it with being able to maintain the vampire's Haven in an undecaying state, and all dots spent on Haven can act in some way (&quot;in some way&quot; meaning I'm not sure how to represent it) to resist damage to it. Also on a passive level, this could protect a torpored vampire's surroundings.</li> <li>The ability to inflict a crushing despair on any mortal who tries to harm the vampire - &quot;this is an immortal thing, bigger than you, older than you, and will be here long after you're gone, how can you hope to stand against it?&quot; - not fear, exactly, that's for Nightmare - but making it existentially hard to try. It could affect mortal supernaturals, but immortal beings should be immune.</li> <li>Precognitive glimpses of the vampire's future - as an unchanging pillar of immortality, all moments of the vampire's existence are one, so the senses that remember their past can be extended to the future as well.</li> <li>The Destined Future Power - as an unchanging pillar of immortality, the vampire bends the fleeting world around itself, drawing events into a pattern according to its will - this means that the future the vampire causes will tend to manifest as circumstances and coincidences more than the vampire's efforts being successful (the world is changing, not the vampire).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Things that make more sense to me as Devotions:<ul><li>Affecting the past. I don't think Chosen Past is the right way to do it exactly, though - if the Discipline draws on the immortality of the vampire, changing the course of their own history seems to weaken the source. Instead, what if they can go back, and &quot;step out&quot; of their timeline, interacting with the world beyond their own actions? As far as that period is concerned, the vampire would be in two places at once - the future self can't affect (or would suffer consequences for affecting) events for their past self, but can interact with the past in other ways, including discovering information and changing the fleeting history of the mortal world. Elders only.</li> <li>Permanence. An always on protection from someone doing the preceding to them. (Which would also act against mages, changelings, or the like doing it to them).</li> <li>Temporal Stasis. Which could in theory act as torpor as well, but with vastly more protection.</li> <li>And of course whatever of the preceding list doesn't make it into the main five.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>And Lastly:</b><br /> <br /> Baldaam once said that when you have a Discipline that any vampire can do, but which is signature for no clan, that suggests an unknown clan. So long as, I suppose, that you can posit a suitable &quot;vampire as...&quot; for it. Which in this case you can. Daevas are vampires as magents of seduction, Gangrel are vampires as savage predators, Mekhet are vampires as occult menace, Nosferatu are vampires as terrors in the shadows, and Venture are vampires as dread lords - but a clan with Eternus can be vampires as the weight of history, which seems both distinct and fitting to the concept of vampires.<br /> <br /> You want to be them because the're eternal - immutable - part of the fabric of the world itself. That's of course also why you should fear them. They should fear themselves because they forget to live - forget what life <i>is</i>.<br /> Losing memories of their mortal life would make sense as the weakness for this clan, making Humanity harder to hold on to.<br /> <br /> Legendary origins might include something to do with the Greek Titans - thrown down by the gods, but too much part of the world to be destroyed, so they endure. Or for the Once Upon a Midnight Darkly collection, well, who do you think first told that story - who was <i>there</i> for ever part of it?<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, Resilience and Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edited to Add:</b><br /> <br /> Whatever else can be said, I find this Discipline very evocative on a conceptual level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the detailed breakdown. Some of that I definitely agree with. I'm thinking more and more I need to, at the least, replace level 4, and turn that solely into a Devotion, maybe as you suggest, working as a sort of 'Shadow' version of yourself tweaking things that are further away from your timeline (with the idea of it instead being best to come into fruition closer to modern times or even in the future). Obfuscate would work as a good secondary there, perhaps.<br /> <br /> I like your musings about a missing clan that perhaps always knew it, although the idea was that in this case, ALL vampires eventually gain it &quot;in-clan&quot; as an elder, because it's at that point as much a part of you as the other clan disciplines tend to be. Still, I could see a clan that always has it, which would make one wonder; what could happen to wipe out a clan who have so cemented themself into the timeline? @_@<br /> <br /> I think I'll go ahead and do a bit of tweaking and see what I come up with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So, I went ahead and nixed chosen past, instead replacing it with Eternal Perfection as a core discipline level for now, with the suggested ability to specifically save actions for any length of time (up to a limited number) instead of it being anything in just the past chapter (it does feel more thematically appropriate).<br /> <br /> I took the suggestion of having a &quot;shadow&quot; projection of your memory being what affects your past. It does make more sense (and is less broken) to have it be unable to affect the Kindred's history directly. Essentially it becomes Schrodinger's gun: the Elder Devotion.<br /> <br /> I tweaked the Inevitable, renaming it and making it a part of Sense of Eternity, at the cost of it being a bit more limited in what it prevents. I'll ponder an ancillary devotion providing this protection to the Kindred's surroundings.<br /> <br /> I wasn't able to think of anything for the preventing mortal from harming idea that wasn't a bit too close to majesty 5 for my liking though.<br /> <br /> Oh and I added a drawback to Sense of Eternity. Something that won't normally be an issue until it is, meaning it's very tempting to just keep it active, but that can definitely hurt you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":